1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:01,964
The fountain, Theo said.

2
00:00:02,404 --> 00:00:05,961
I stared at him. Big tank underneath, Theo
said.

3
00:00:06,331 --> 00:00:08,151
There's a room with all the pumps.

4
00:00:08,171 --> 00:00:10,591
Number's written on the side.

5
00:00:10,952 --> 00:00:12,512
Eight thousand? He nodded.

6
00:00:12,892 --> 00:00:14,632
I knew the pump-room door.

7
00:00:14,952 --> 00:00:17,892
It opened into the center court, beside
the pretzel place.

8
00:00:18,212 --> 00:00:21,772
On the cameras, that doorway was buried
behind bodies.

9
00:00:22,092 --> 00:00:23,572
The way downstairs is full.

10
00:00:23,932 --> 00:00:27,935
I come from above. He drew a route in the
chalk with one finger.

11
00:00:29,075 --> 00:00:31,755
Above the cinema. Across a service
walkway.

12
00:00:31,955 --> 00:00:35,355
Down inside the big column beside the
fountain, on a maintenance ladder.

13
00:00:35,795 --> 00:00:38,035
The route ended behind the locked
pump-room door.

14
00:00:38,315 --> 00:00:40,175
I could feel the weight of the keys on my
hip.

15
00:00:40,575 --> 00:00:43,454
Why haven't you gone already? Nothing to
carry it in.

16
00:00:43,756 --> 00:00:48,216
The store around us was full of camping
water containers.

17
00:00:48,936 --> 00:00:50,756
How much can you carry back?

18
00:00:51,096 --> 00:00:53,796
I asked. He held his hands a little apart.

19
00:00:54,190 --> 00:00:56,870
Small ones. You have to get them through.

20
00:00:57,362 --> 00:00:59,062
We settled on two smaller ones.

21
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:01,980
Theo watched without saying anything.

22
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:03,580
I wished he'd made a joke.

23
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:07,020
It would've been easier than watching him
decide whether I could do it.

24
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,000
He looked at them. Looked at me.

25
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,620
We understood each other then.

26
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:13,240
I'd been counting bottles and locking
gates.

27
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:15,300
He'd been counting routes through walls.

28
00:01:15,766 --> 00:01:17,586
That night Vera called again.

29
00:01:17,986 --> 00:01:20,906
She said the little girl had stopped
asking for food.

30
00:01:21,266 --> 00:01:24,386
I held the radio so tightly the plastic
creaked.

31
00:01:24,706 --> 00:01:27,159
Get some sleep, Danny, she said.

32
00:01:27,473 --> 00:01:28,833
You'll think better tomorrow.

33
00:01:29,394 --> 00:01:33,134
I sat beside Theo's bucket after the light
went out.

34
00:01:33,374 --> 00:01:35,034
Show me the way, I said.

35
00:01:35,314 --> 00:01:37,554
We bring water back. You get food.

36
00:01:37,854 --> 00:01:39,134
We work the rest out after.

37
00:01:39,374 --> 00:01:41,274
He looked at the tent, then at the rack.

38
00:01:41,672 --> 00:01:45,032
My mom had gone into the apartment with
about ten days of insulin.

39
00:01:45,352 --> 00:01:49,252
Every time I counted my water, I found
myself counting her days too.

40
00:01:49,581 --> 00:01:52,281
Getting more water wouldn't get me across
the highway.

41
00:01:52,641 --> 00:01:56,621
But I couldn't do anything for either of
them if I spent the next week

42
00:01:56,641 --> 00:01:58,521
getting too weak to climb the roof ladder.

43
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:00,297
You coming too? Yes.

44
00:02:00,577 --> 00:02:04,217
He glanced at my boots. That was when I
started worrying about what his route

45
00:02:04,237 --> 00:02:04,937
could hold.

46
00:02:06,073 --> 00:02:07,793
We left before the mall got bright.

47
00:02:08,173 --> 00:02:12,393
I took empty camping containers, a
flashlight, and a strap from the climbing

48
00:02:12,413 --> 00:02:15,193
display. I took the battery out of
Marcus's radio.

49
00:02:15,413 --> 00:02:18,253
Wrapped the keyring in a sock so the metal
would stay quiet.

50
00:02:18,695 --> 00:02:22,055
Theo made me try the rack without the
containers first.

51
00:02:22,395 --> 00:02:25,255
On the second shelf I reached for
something that looked solid.

52
00:02:25,555 --> 00:02:27,755
He caught my hand before I put any weight
on it.

53
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,754
That's for holding the ceiling up, he
said.

54
00:02:31,170 --> 00:02:36,308
It won't hold you. He moved my hand to a
thick support above it.

55
00:02:36,668 --> 00:02:39,347
I nodded as if I'd understood that all
along.

56
00:02:39,470 --> 00:02:40,720
You always carry that many?

57
00:02:41,092 --> 00:02:43,401
Every night. Must've been annoying.

58
00:02:43,877 --> 00:02:48,257
It had been. I would've given almost
anything to be annoyed by that sound

59
00:02:48,277 --> 00:02:50,317
again on an ordinary Tuesday.

60
00:02:51,297 --> 00:02:55,517
Above the store, the air was warm and
smelled like dust from a heater

61
00:02:55,537 --> 00:02:57,057
somebody had just switched on.

62
00:02:57,397 --> 00:02:59,417
Theo showed me where the metal supports
ran.

63
00:02:59,751 --> 00:03:02,171
I followed them on my hands and knees.

64
00:03:02,191 --> 00:03:04,671
Kept my weight on the heavy steel.

65
00:03:04,691 --> 00:03:08,411
The ceiling tiles shifted below us when I
breathed too hard.

66
00:03:09,031 --> 00:03:12,031
Over the cinema, he stopped beside a
stained blanket.

67
00:03:12,411 --> 00:03:17,291
There were three empty water bottles, a
folded hoodie, and a photograph

68
00:03:17,311 --> 00:03:18,511
turned face down.

69
00:03:18,791 --> 00:03:21,331
He slid that underneath the blanket before
I could see it.

70
00:03:21,619 --> 00:03:27,099
A door beside the little platform had
CINEMA SERVICE stencilled across it.

71
00:03:27,419 --> 00:03:30,959
Key seventeen fit. Theo watched the lock
turn as though I'd done a trick.

72
00:03:31,359 --> 00:03:32,659
You've been climbing around this?

73
00:03:33,011 --> 00:03:37,066
For a while. I opened it just wide enough
for us to get through.

74
00:03:37,466 --> 00:03:40,766
On the other side was the service walkway
over the center court.

75
00:03:41,206 --> 00:03:44,086
Through gaps beneath the rail, I could see
the tops of heads.

76
00:03:44,706 --> 00:03:48,406
Theo stepped out first. Halfway across,
the proper walkway ended.

77
00:03:48,686 --> 00:03:52,406
Beyond it, the route followed a pair of
supports above the suspended ceiling.

78
00:03:52,766 --> 00:03:54,800
I stopped. Theo looked back.

79
00:03:55,207 --> 00:03:58,107
Don't put your foot where you think the
floor is.

80
00:03:59,451 --> 00:04:03,691
My best friend walked his rounds while I
crawled over his head.

81
00:04:04,551 --> 00:04:06,051
Theo crossed the first gap easily.

82
00:04:06,451 --> 00:04:09,951
I watched where his hands went, then tried
to put mine in the same places.

83
00:04:10,711 --> 00:04:14,011
There was a difference between watching a
skinny fifteen-year-old do

84
00:04:14,031 --> 00:04:16,811
something and asking my knees to do it
afterward.

85
00:04:17,294 --> 00:04:18,954
Sweat ran down my nose.

86
00:04:19,314 --> 00:04:21,554
I caught it on my sleeve before it could
fall.

87
00:04:21,934 --> 00:04:24,494
One of the emergency lights flickered
underneath us.

88
00:04:24,694 --> 00:04:28,414
For a second the shadows moved and I
tightened both hands on the steel.

89
00:04:28,874 --> 00:04:31,014
Theo stopped with me. He didn't tell me to
hurry.

90
00:04:31,318 --> 00:04:33,115
Next hand, he whispered.

91
00:04:33,455 --> 00:04:35,308
I moved it. Now your knee.

92
00:04:35,676 --> 00:04:40,196
I moved that too. After a while I could do
two movements without being told.

93
00:04:40,556 --> 00:04:42,056
I was grateful he didn't mention it.

94
00:04:42,176 --> 00:04:43,956
Below us, the fountain was dark.

95
00:04:44,456 --> 00:04:47,736
Coins lay on the bottom. The people around
it were standing shoulder to

96
00:04:47,756 --> 00:04:51,356
shoulder in places, their faces turned
toward the food-court doors.

97
00:04:51,656 --> 00:04:52,976
I stopped counting at a hundred.

98
00:04:53,290 --> 00:04:55,230
Theo reached back for a container.

99
00:04:55,690 --> 00:04:59,650
I passed it forward. He put it on a solid
section, then came back for the

100
00:04:59,670 --> 00:05:00,850
other one. Slow.

101
00:05:01,210 --> 00:05:02,650
Everything had to be slow.

102
00:05:02,910 --> 00:05:04,830
A gate rattled at the far end of the hall.

103
00:05:05,090 --> 00:05:06,950
I knew who it was before I saw him.

104
00:05:07,179 --> 00:05:10,329
Marcus came around the corner and stopped
at the first store.

105
00:05:10,639 --> 00:05:12,419
Two pulls on the gate. A pause.

106
00:05:12,799 --> 00:05:15,699
Then the next one. I found myself waiting
for him to look up.

107
00:05:16,199 --> 00:05:18,999
Theo touched my shoulder. I moved my knee
to give him room.

108
00:05:19,259 --> 00:05:20,759
The bit of metal under it folded.

109
00:05:21,169 --> 00:05:25,029
I dropped far enough that my stomach hit
the edge of the support.

110
00:05:25,349 --> 00:05:27,109
My right leg punched through a tile.

111
00:05:27,509 --> 00:05:30,049
Something caught the leather of my boot
and held it there.

112
00:05:30,329 --> 00:05:31,689
Pieces fell into the court.

113
00:05:31,909 --> 00:05:33,689
The first one struck the fountain's rim.

114
00:05:33,989 --> 00:05:35,389
A head turned. Then another.

115
00:05:35,795 --> 00:05:37,015
Theo caught my wrist.

116
00:05:37,495 --> 00:05:41,375
I tried to pull my knee back, and a sharp
edge dug into my thigh.

117
00:05:41,715 --> 00:05:43,435
Below, Marcus stopped walking.

118
00:05:43,715 --> 00:05:45,575
He lifted his face toward my foot.

119
00:05:45,875 --> 00:05:47,815
My boot began to slide off.

120
00:05:49,198 --> 00:05:53,218
The kid I'd told to leave was the only
thing keeping me out of that crowd.

121
00:05:53,738 --> 00:05:56,338
Theo lay flat and reached for my other
wrist.

122
00:05:56,658 --> 00:05:58,438
His fingers slipped on my sleeve.

123
00:05:58,848 --> 00:06:01,357
Give me your hand. I tried.

124
00:06:02,117 --> 00:06:06,037
A long piece of the tile broke away and
hit someone's shoulder.

125
00:06:06,997 --> 00:06:08,877
People began pushing under the hole.

126
00:06:10,137 --> 00:06:12,577
Slowly, one body leaning into the next.

127
00:06:13,137 --> 00:06:15,137
Marcus stood among them, looking up.

128
00:06:15,448 --> 00:06:17,608
I could see the worn patch on his cap.

129
00:06:17,948 --> 00:06:21,528
I'd stood beside him in the office while
he picked at it with his thumbnail

130
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:23,928
and told me a joke I'd already heard.

131
00:06:24,208 --> 00:06:26,748
I nearly said his name. Theo hit my arm.

132
00:06:27,068 --> 00:06:28,596
Look at me. I looked up.

133
00:06:28,916 --> 00:06:30,796
He was reaching for the strap I'd brought.

134
00:06:31,056 --> 00:06:35,036
Getting it around the heavy support with
one hand while the other held my

135
00:06:35,056 --> 00:06:38,499
sleeve. You have to let go, he whispered.

136
00:06:39,179 --> 00:06:41,373
I shook my head. One hand.

137
00:06:41,793 --> 00:06:46,245
I need the strap. His sleeve was bunched
in my fist.

138
00:06:47,245 --> 00:06:50,345
I'd been holding him so hard the cloth had
twisted around his arm.

139
00:06:51,085 --> 00:06:52,545
I made myself open my fingers.

140
00:06:52,885 --> 00:06:55,725
He fed the strap around the support and
leaned his weight into it.

141
00:06:55,905 --> 00:06:57,625
I heard fabric pull tight.

142
00:06:57,805 --> 00:07:01,065
His shoe slipped against the brace, and he
caught himself with a sharp little

143
00:07:01,085 --> 00:07:04,667
breath. Then his hand was back in front of
my face.

144
00:07:05,067 --> 00:07:06,842
Elbow up, he said.

145
00:07:07,377 --> 00:07:11,112
You have to help. I got an elbow onto the
steel.

146
00:07:11,492 --> 00:07:14,592
Pushed until my shoulder felt as though it
was coming apart.

147
00:07:15,112 --> 00:07:17,592
Theo leaned back against the strap and
pulled.

148
00:07:18,092 --> 00:07:19,532
My boot stayed where it was.

149
00:07:19,852 --> 00:07:21,132
My foot came out of it.

150
00:07:21,352 --> 00:07:23,432
For a second I thought that meant I was
falling.

151
00:07:23,890 --> 00:07:29,130
Then my knee slid over the edge, and Theo
dragged me onto the solid platform

152
00:07:29,150 --> 00:07:32,470
with him. We lay there together, breathing
into our sleeves.

153
00:07:32,890 --> 00:07:35,610
Below us, the boot finally came loose.

154
00:07:36,030 --> 00:07:39,090
It landed inside the empty fountain with a
noise that seemed to go on

155
00:07:39,110 --> 00:07:42,790
forever. Theo pressed both palms against
the metal and waited.

156
00:07:43,186 --> 00:07:45,906
Eventually the pushing slowed.

157
00:07:46,506 --> 00:07:47,946
A few faces turned away.

158
00:07:48,266 --> 00:07:51,666
I looked at him. His trouser leg was torn
at the calf.

159
00:07:52,026 --> 00:07:56,086
There was blood on the sharp brace he'd
crawled across to reach me.

160
00:07:56,286 --> 00:07:57,886
He pulled the fabric down over it.

161
00:07:58,185 --> 00:08:01,305
You can walk without that shoe, he
whispered.

162
00:08:01,665 --> 00:08:05,285
Somewhere ahead and below us, water
dripped.

163
00:08:06,567 --> 00:08:09,367
The maintenance ladder ran down inside the
service column.

164
00:08:09,647 --> 00:08:13,387
At the bottom, a narrow hatch opened into
the pump room beneath the fountain.

165
00:08:13,788 --> 00:08:16,708
I put my good foot on each rung first.

166
00:08:17,148 --> 00:08:20,688
Theo stayed close enough to hear every
breath I was trying to keep quiet.

167
00:08:21,008 --> 00:08:22,528
The tank took up most of the room.

168
00:08:22,548 --> 00:08:27,228
EIGHT THOUSAND GALLONS was printed on a
plate beside its inspection window.

169
00:08:27,708 --> 00:08:29,028
There was water behind the glass.

170
00:08:29,418 --> 00:08:33,398
I put my hand against the tank and left it
there for a while.

171
00:08:33,718 --> 00:08:37,018
We still had to get it back and treat it
with the gear in the store.

172
00:08:37,738 --> 00:08:41,218
But I could stop staring at the last few
bottles every time I swallowed.

173
00:08:42,038 --> 00:08:44,438
Theo eased himself onto the bottom rung.

174
00:08:44,658 --> 00:08:45,918
He was favouring his leg.

175
00:08:46,338 --> 00:08:47,925
You hurt? Caught it.

176
00:08:48,159 --> 00:08:50,215
I saw. Then why'd you ask?

177
00:08:50,584 --> 00:08:53,744
I nearly smiled. We filled what we could
carry.

178
00:08:54,424 --> 00:08:57,984
The handles pulled at my fingers when I
lifted the containers.

179
00:08:58,744 --> 00:09:01,244
We'd be drinking what we carried back for
days.

180
00:09:01,844 --> 00:09:04,184
After that, we'd have to come again.

181
00:09:04,584 --> 00:09:07,384
The thought of that crossing again made me
put one down.

182
00:09:08,084 --> 00:09:12,272
Theo noticed. We can find a better bit to
cross, he said.

183
00:09:13,072 --> 00:09:14,975
You know one? I can look.

184
00:09:15,512 --> 00:09:16,892
I held the handle again.

185
00:09:17,232 --> 00:09:21,032
He'd spent four months figuring this place
out because he had to.

186
00:09:21,672 --> 00:09:23,452
I was going to have to start doing the
same.

187
00:09:24,132 --> 00:09:27,832
Outside the pump-room door, a shoe scraped
along the floor.

188
00:09:28,152 --> 00:09:29,712
Dust shook out of the frame.

189
00:09:30,132 --> 00:09:31,592
Theo stared at that door.

190
00:09:31,929 --> 00:09:33,937
This is where they were, he said.

191
00:09:34,337 --> 00:09:36,102
Who? The drill people.

192
00:09:36,603 --> 00:09:38,363
I set the container down.

193
00:09:38,670 --> 00:09:41,230
Three of them. A woman and two men.

194
00:09:41,530 --> 00:09:42,750
Behind the pretzel place.

195
00:09:43,190 --> 00:09:45,090
First night. What time?

196
00:09:45,551 --> 00:09:48,511
One-thirty. I could see the clock through
the opening.

197
00:09:48,855 --> 00:09:52,975
One-thirty. Ten minutes before Marcus
called about the man on the ramp.

198
00:09:53,304 --> 00:09:54,684
They were cutting through the wall.
